WEBVTT

00:00:00.417 --> 00:00:04.658
Last updated: 11 August 20 26

00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:07.768
The short version.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:11.841
The documents, images, videos and files

00:00:11.909 --> 00:00:15.144
you make in Lolly stay on your device.

00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:19.123
There are no accounts for ordinary use, no

00:00:19.192 --> 00:00:21.386
cookies from the app itself and no

00:00:21.444 --> 00:00:23.734
analytics or trackers anywhere in the

00:00:23.795 --> 00:00:27.288
codebase - not "we don't use the data,"

00:00:27.351 --> 00:00:30.294
genuinely not present in the source.

00:00:31.056 --> 00:00:33.414
A short, complete list of exceptions

00:00:33.479 --> 00:00:36.062
exists where the software talks to a

00:00:36.121 --> 00:00:39.077
network at all, and every one of them is

00:00:39.137 --> 00:00:42.611
described below in specifics: what leaves,

00:00:42.693 --> 00:00:44.570
to whom and when.

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:48.149
The only exception that involves anything

00:00:48.211 --> 00:00:51.113
personal is a sign-in you have to

00:00:51.172 --> 00:00:53.119
explicitly start.

00:00:53.884 --> 00:00:56.859
If it isn't in this document, it doesn't

00:00:56.921 --> 00:00:58.019
happen.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.641
What this policy covers

00:01:02.608 --> 00:01:05.972
Lolly is open-source software - an engine,

00:01:06.059 --> 00:01:08.949
several app shells «web, desktop, mobile,

00:01:09.029 --> 00:01:11.914
CLI» and a browser extension - that anyone

00:01:11.974 --> 00:01:13.270
can run.

00:01:14.045 --> 00:01:16.918
This policy has two parts:

00:01:17.687 --> 00:01:20.399
The software itself: what it does and

00:01:20.452 --> 00:01:23.320
doesn't do with your data, wherever it

00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:25.542
runs.

00:01:26.316 --> 00:01:29.278
This is a property of the code, so it's

00:01:29.359 --> 00:01:32.294
true of every Lolly deployment, ours or

00:01:32.364 --> 00:01:33.994
anyone else's.

00:01:34.785 --> 00:01:37.659
lolly-tools, the reference deployment SUSE

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.556
operates: the specific choices

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.877
made running its optional server-side

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.848
pieces «what's logged, for how long, by

00:01:46.908 --> 00:01:47.895
whom».

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:50.997
If you're using a self-hosted or

00:01:51.062 --> 00:01:53.838
enterprise Lolly instance, the software

00:01:53.898 --> 00:01:56.855
behaviour below still applies, but the

00:01:56.946 --> 00:01:59.902
operator of that instance - not SUSE - is

00:01:59.954 --> 00:02:03.194
responsible for anything server-side:

00:02:03.259 --> 00:02:06.584
their render endpoint, their MCP server,

00:02:06.646 --> 00:02:08.805
their Content Credentials certificate

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.644
authority, if they run one.

00:02:12.426 --> 00:02:15.494
Ask them for their own policy.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.046
See Adoption & Governance for what

00:02:19.128 --> 00:02:21.569
operating Lolly involves.

00:02:22.706 --> 00:02:25.719
The app: what stays on your device

00:02:26.731 --> 00:02:29.812
Lolly's web, desktop and mobile shells run

00:02:29.871 --> 00:02:33.269
the entire render engine client-side.

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.856
Opening a tool, filling in inputs,

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.487
previewing and exporting all happen on

00:02:39.549 --> 00:02:42.825
your device - no server is involved, and

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.845
the app works offline once loaded.

00:02:46.638 --> 00:02:49.368
The app sets no cookies.

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:53.007
To function, it keeps a small amount of

00:02:53.069 --> 00:02:55.720
data on your device only, never

00:02:55.782 --> 00:02:57.269
transmitted:

00:02:58.028 --> 00:03:00.783
Interface preferences - theme, language,

00:03:00.844 --> 00:03:03.725
sound settings, sidebar/zoom

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.411
sizing, sort and view choices, which

00:03:07.503 --> 00:03:09.388
onboarding tips you've seen - in

00:03:09.449 --> 00:03:12.569
localStorage, so they're available before

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:15.019
the app has finished booting.

00:03:15.805 --> 00:03:18.883
An offline cache of the tool catalogue and

00:03:18.953 --> 00:03:21.805
asset previews, so the gallery

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.467
works without a connection.

00:03:26.258 --> 00:03:29.122
Local usage counters for your profile

00:03:29.188 --> 00:03:32.250
card's stats «how many exports, which

00:03:33.185 --> 00:03:35.468
tools» - a small bounded blob in

00:03:35.529 --> 00:03:39.131
localStorage, never read by us, never sent

00:03:39.198 --> 00:03:40.394
anywhere.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.577
Your own documents, saved sessions,

00:03:43.636 --> 00:03:46.644
uploaded assets and fonts - stored in

00:03:47.528 --> 00:03:51.083
IndexedDB on your device, never uploaded,

00:03:51.147 --> 00:03:53.819
never read by anyone but you.

00:03:54.612 --> 00:03:57.549
None of this is shared, sold or used to

00:03:57.609 --> 00:03:59.845
identify or track you.

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:03.447
There is nothing to consent to, because

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:06.016
there is no collection happening - only

00:04:06.078 --> 00:04:09.053
this notice, so you know what's kept and

00:04:09.118 --> 00:04:10.169
where.

00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:14.619
Wipe all of it at any time with Profile →

00:04:14.702 --> 00:04:17.771
Clear all my data, or by clearing the

00:04:17.862 --> 00:04:20.545
site's storage in your browser.

00:04:21.326 --> 00:04:25.168
«Under the ePrivacy Directive Art.

00:04:25.947 --> 00:04:29.130
5«3», storage that is strictly necessary

00:04:29.253 --> 00:04:32.121
for the service you asked for doesn't

00:04:32.163 --> 00:04:35.700
require consent - only transparency, which

00:04:35.762 --> 00:04:38.101
is what this document and the in-app

00:04:38.192 --> 00:04:40.119
notice both are.»

00:04:40.903 --> 00:04:43.493
Your own backup of this data - the

00:04:43.579 --> 00:04:46.529
lolly-backup bundle produced by Export my

00:04:46.589 --> 00:04:50.169
data & render everything - is a file you

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.120
keep and control.

00:04:52.871 --> 00:04:55.627
It never touches our servers unless you

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.844
choose to send it somewhere yourself.

00:04:59.642 --> 00:05:02.194
See Data Transfer.

00:05:03.323 --> 00:05:05.841
On-device utilities

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:09.708
Some tools - Strip Hidden Data, Compress

00:05:09.793 --> 00:05:12.851
PDF and others carrying the "Runs on your

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:15.784
device" badge - operate on a file you

00:05:15.841 --> 00:05:17.094
provide.

00:05:17.874 --> 00:05:20.426
The file is read into memory in your

00:05:20.489 --> 00:05:23.711
browser, transformed locally and offered

00:05:23.773 --> 00:05:25.944
back as a download.

00:05:26.695 --> 00:05:29.427
It is never uploaded, because there is no

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.894
server in the path to upload it to.

00:05:33.668 --> 00:05:36.540
These utilities work offline, and their

00:05:36.629 --> 00:05:40.043
output carries no watermark or metadata of

00:05:40.137 --> 00:05:42.976
ours - the point of most of them is to

00:05:43.035 --> 00:05:46.845
remove & protect data, not add risk.

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:50.573
When the app talks to a network, in full

00:05:51.436 --> 00:05:54.328
The table below is the complete list of

00:05:54.424 --> 00:05:57.636
everything the app fetches or sends over a

00:05:57.697 --> 00:05:58.869
network.

00:05:59.618 --> 00:06:03.120
If it isn't here, the app doesn't do it.

00:06:03.888 --> 00:06:06.984
Every fixed host in that table is also the

00:06:07.046 --> 00:06:09.141
complete allowlist in the app's

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:12.443
Content-Security-Policy, which the browser

00:06:12.507 --> 00:06:14.019
enforces.

00:06:14.803 --> 00:06:17.641
So the list is not only a description of

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:20.346
what the code does today, it is the

00:06:20.425 --> 00:06:23.810
boundary the browser holds the app to: a

00:06:23.894 --> 00:06:26.632
future change that tried to contact some

00:06:26.668 --> 00:06:29.469
other host would be blocked, not silently

00:06:29.529 --> 00:06:30.745
permitted.

00:06:31.537 --> 00:06:34.450
One row is the deliberate exception, and

00:06:34.504 --> 00:06:37.753
its own cell says so: Send to LinkedIn

00:06:37.796 --> 00:06:40.996
exists in the desktop apps only, so the

00:06:41.085 --> 00:06:43.620
web app's policy names neither of its

00:06:43.681 --> 00:06:46.336
hosts - the web app could not reach them

00:06:46.441 --> 00:06:48.919
even if its code tried.

00:06:49.693 --> 00:06:52.664
Two more rows have no fixed host, because

00:06:52.726 --> 00:06:55.043
you choose the address at the moment of

00:06:55.109 --> 00:06:59.293
use: a URL you ask a tool to capture, and

00:06:59.352 --> 00:07:02.645
a remote instance you point the shell at.

00:07:03.431 --> 00:07:06.717
Neither is in the policy, and each happens

00:07:06.807 --> 00:07:09.689
only when you type an address and act on

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.669
it.

00:07:11.434 --> 00:07:13.661
A deployment that wants none of the

00:07:13.749 --> 00:07:16.563
optional ones «an enterprise instance with

00:07:16.623 --> 00:07:19.972
its own fonts, say» removes those hosts

00:07:20.059 --> 00:07:22.982
from its policy and the features fail

00:07:23.066 --> 00:07:25.745
closed rather than reaching out.

00:07:26.543 --> 00:07:28.761
None of these send your documents,

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:31.640
projects, sessions or uploaded files

00:07:31.711 --> 00:07:32.894
anywhere.

00:07:33.654 --> 00:07:36.263
They exist to bring things to your device

00:07:36.325 --> 00:07:39.336
«tools, fonts, models», never to send

00:07:39.397 --> 00:07:42.376
things from it, with the exceptions named

00:07:42.455 --> 00:07:45.445
explicitly in the sections below.

00:07:46.225 --> 00:07:49.418
A note on what we removed.

00:07:50.192 --> 00:07:53.551
Verify can check SEAL signatures, a scheme

00:07:53.611 --> 00:07:56.416
where a file's signing key is published in

00:07:56.478 --> 00:07:57.794
DNS.

00:07:58.556 --> 00:08:02.112
Browsers can't make DNS queries, so any

00:08:02.174 --> 00:08:04.929
web implementation has to route the lookup

00:08:05.023 --> 00:08:08.372
through a third-party DNS-over-HTTPS

00:08:08.432 --> 00:08:11.294
resolver - which would show that operator

00:08:11.354 --> 00:08:14.114
the domain being checked plus your IP

00:08:14.172 --> 00:08:15.345
address.

00:08:16.141 --> 00:08:19.218
We used to use Cloudflare's.

00:08:19.982 --> 00:08:22.058
We don't any more, and there is no

00:08:22.113 --> 00:08:25.168
replacement: the web app now passes no

00:08:25.228 --> 00:08:28.506
resolver at all, so SEAL verification here

00:08:28.566 --> 00:08:31.245
makes zero network requests.

00:08:32.024 --> 00:08:34.904
Files whose SEAL record carries its key

00:08:34.968 --> 00:08:38.718
inline still verify completely offline.

00:08:39.487 --> 00:08:42.753
Files whose key lives in DNS report "no

00:08:42.840 --> 00:08:45.854
key resolver" instead, and you can check

00:08:45.914 --> 00:08:49.188
those in the desktop or command-line app,

00:08:49.246 --> 00:08:52.013
which resolve DNS natively through your

00:08:52.075 --> 00:08:55.570
own machine with no third party involved.

00:08:56.349 --> 00:08:59.245
You can confirm this yourself: greppable

00:08:59.306 --> 00:09:01.809
checks for this and every other claim on

00:09:01.855 --> 00:09:04.836
this page, with the exact commands and

00:09:04.891 --> 00:09:07.929
expected output, live at Verify It

00:09:07.978 --> 00:09:09.220
Yourself.

00:09:10.356 --> 00:09:12.729
Hot-linked render URL'S

00:09:13.697 --> 00:09:17.143
Currently switched off on lolly-tools.

00:09:17.926 --> 00:09:20.168
Every lolly-tools>.

00:09:20.969 --> 00:09:25.093
URL returns 404 today.

00:09:25.859 --> 00:09:28.229
The section below describes what the

00:09:28.323 --> 00:09:31.672
feature does when an operator enables it,

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:33.720
and why we have not.

00:09:34.469 --> 00:09:37.205
It will be turned on here once the service

00:09:37.282 --> 00:09:40.720
moves to SUSE-operated infrastructure, and

00:09:40.777 --> 00:09:43.970
this notice will change when it is.

00:09:44.746 --> 00:09:47.726
The app itself stays entirely on your

00:09:47.787 --> 00:09:49.019
device.

00:09:49.808 --> 00:09:52.345
Separately, an operator can enable

00:09:52.435 --> 00:09:55.994
hot-link render URL'S - /tool/ .

00:09:56.766 --> 00:09:56.840
?

00:09:57.591 --> 00:10:00.483
- so a shared Lolly link can appear as a

00:10:00.545 --> 00:10:03.707
live image in a README, a wiki or a

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:05.119
dashboard.

00:10:05.891 --> 00:10:08.580
Fetching one asks the server to render

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:11.777
public tool and catalogue data with the

00:10:11.853 --> 00:10:14.794
inputs written into the URL.

00:10:15.589 --> 00:10:18.794
No accounts, no cookies, no state.

00:10:19.571 --> 00:10:23.093
The endpoint is anonymous, and nothing

00:10:23.987 --> 00:10:26.868
on your device is read.

00:10:27.648 --> 00:10:30.792
Your documents, sessions and uploads never

00:10:30.853 --> 00:10:33.294
leave your browser - they cannot appear in

00:10:33.355 --> 00:10:35.194
these links at all.

00:10:35.961 --> 00:10:39.644
But the URL itself is recorded.

00:10:40.417 --> 00:10:43.182
A URL'S query string is part of the

00:10:43.242 --> 00:10:44.305
request

00:10:45.349 --> 00:10:47.846
line, so it shows up in the hosting

00:10:47.908 --> 00:10:51.297
platform's ordinary access logs the same

00:10:51.359 --> 00:10:54.319
way every requested path does.

00:10:55.077 --> 00:10:57.820
If a link's inputs contain someone's name

00:10:57.877 --> 00:11:01.090
or email - a name badge, an email

00:11:01.183 --> 00:11:04.468
signature - that text sits in those logs,

00:11:04.529 --> 00:11:07.251
and no amount of policy wording changes

00:11:07.313 --> 00:11:08.244
it.

00:11:09.029 --> 00:11:12.131
This is the specific reason the feature is

00:11:12.193 --> 00:11:14.568
off here rather than on.

00:11:15.343 --> 00:11:17.962
The inputs are public by construction

00:11:18.059 --> 00:11:20.911
anyway - they are whatever the link's

00:11:21.863 --> 00:11:25.120
author typed into the URL, readable by

00:11:25.209 --> 00:11:27.594
anyone the link reaches.

00:11:28.366 --> 00:11:31.644
Don't put secrets in a shared link.

00:11:32.445 --> 00:11:35.739
Lolly offers link encryption for sensitive

00:11:35.803 --> 00:11:37.144
content.

00:11:37.923 --> 00:11:40.946
Responses are cached and rate-limited like

00:11:41.001 --> 00:11:43.879
any public image, and marked

00:11:44.889 --> 00:11:48.221
noindex so search engines don't index your

00:11:48.282 --> 00:11:49.494
renders.

00:11:50.282 --> 00:11:53.326
Self-hosting Lolly and don't want a public

00:11:53.387 --> 00:11:55.069
render surface?

00:11:55.852 --> 00:11:59.114
Set LOLLY_DISABLE_RENDER_GET=1 - what

00:11:59.173 --> 00:12:02.381
lolly-tools itself currently does - and

00:12:02.478 --> 00:12:06.545
every one of these URL'S returns 404.

00:12:07.669 --> 00:12:12.001
The MCP server «optional, for AI agents»

00:12:12.972 --> 00:12:16.439
Lolly can also be reached by an AI agent

00:12:16.506 --> 00:12:19.414
over the Model Context Protocol - an

00:12:19.501 --> 00:12:22.200
operator-run endpoint «lolly-tools runs

00:12:22.266 --> 00:12:25.769
one; anyone can self-host their own,

00:12:25.832 --> 00:12:28.244
including fully air-gapped».

00:12:28.997 --> 00:12:31.646
It shares the render path's no-accounts

00:12:31.708 --> 00:12:34.924
posture, plus three tools that necessarily

00:12:34.989 --> 00:12:36.944
handle file bytes:

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.848
lolly_transform «run an on-device utility

00:12:40.932 --> 00:12:43.483
server-side, on the calling

00:12:44.352 --> 00:12:46.973
agent's behalf», lolly_verify «check

00:12:47.033 --> 00:12:49.945
Content Credentials» and lolly_redact

00:12:50.005 --> 00:12:53.605
«black out regions of an image or PDF» all

00:12:53.663 --> 00:12:56.895
accept a file's bytes from the caller.

00:12:57.655 --> 00:13:00.879
They are processed in-process, in memory,

00:13:00.941 --> 00:13:03.582
and the result is returned in that same

00:13:03.652 --> 00:13:06.671
call - the file is never written to disk

00:13:06.758 --> 00:13:08.767
and never stored once the request

00:13:08.827 --> 00:13:10.070
completes.

00:13:10.825 --> 00:13:12.780
Every other tool - lolly_render,

00:13:12.844 --> 00:13:16.020
lolly_build_url, lolly_list_tools,

00:13:16.807 --> 00:13:18.788
lolly_describe_tool - works from

00:13:18.848 --> 00:13:22.260
parameters only «text, numbers, colours,

00:13:22.338 --> 00:13:25.493
URL'S, catalogue asset ids», the same

00:13:25.554 --> 00:13:28.970
inputs a hot-link render URL takes.

00:13:29.733 --> 00:13:32.176
Access is either a shared token the

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:35.178
operator issues to clients they trust, or

00:13:36.207 --> 00:13:39.598
stateless OAuth 2 point 1: short-lived

00:13:39.685 --> 00:13:42.425
signed tokens verified against a shared

00:13:42.511 --> 00:13:45.737
secret, nothing stored server-side and the

00:13:45.802 --> 00:13:48.932
token itself is never written to a log or

00:13:48.986 --> 00:13:51.044
a render URL.

00:13:52.146 --> 00:13:55.343
Content Credentials identity «a sign-in

00:13:55.394 --> 00:13:57.592
you have to start yourself»

00:13:58.565 --> 00:14:01.298
Lolly can seal a cryptographic Content

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.725
Credential into your exports so anyone can

00:14:04.787 --> 00:14:08.617
verify, offline, that a file is unaltered

00:14:08.680 --> 00:14:10.644
since it left Lolly.

00:14:11.411 --> 00:14:14.765
That much is on by default and fully local

00:14:14.849 --> 00:14:17.548
- the signing key is generated on your

00:14:17.608 --> 00:14:21.395
device and signing itself happens offline.

00:14:22.153 --> 00:14:25.491
Without enrolment that key is a throwaway:

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:28.527
a fresh keypair minted for each export and

00:14:28.592 --> 00:14:30.169
dropped with it.

00:14:30.938 --> 00:14:34.019
Once you enrol, the key becomes a lasting

00:14:34.079 --> 00:14:37.250
one and is generated non-extractable - not

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.580
even Lolly's own code can read it, only

00:14:40.657 --> 00:14:42.620
ask it to sign.

00:14:43.406 --> 00:14:47.068
Either way it never leaves your device.

00:14:47.844 --> 00:14:50.515
This section covers the one optional step

00:14:50.554 --> 00:14:53.779
on top of that: enrolling a verified

00:14:53.841 --> 00:14:57.350
identity, so your exports say "Verified -

00:14:57.415 --> 00:15:02.094
signed by \ " instead of an anonymous key.

00:15:02.845 --> 00:15:05.338
If you skip enrolment, nothing in this

00:15:05.405 --> 00:15:08.369
section applies to you, and no personal

00:15:08.430 --> 00:15:11.095
data ever leaves your device.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.849
If you do enrol, here is exactly what

00:15:14.911 --> 00:15:16.168
happens:

00:15:16.957 --> 00:15:19.504
You choose a sign-in method - GitHub,

00:15:19.568 --> 00:15:22.450
Google, SUSE «id-suse-com» or an

00:15:23.451 --> 00:15:25.319
emailed link.

00:15:26.101 --> 00:15:28.637
For the three OIDC providers, you're

00:15:28.703 --> 00:15:31.618
redirected to that provider's own login

00:15:31.682 --> 00:15:34.732
page, governed by their privacy policy,

00:15:34.789 --> 00:15:36.294
not ours.

00:15:37.082 --> 00:15:39.752
Lolly's certificate service receives back

00:15:39.846 --> 00:15:42.924
only a verified email address and the

00:15:42.984 --> 00:15:44.670
provider's name.

00:15:45.448 --> 00:15:47.956
For the email link, the address you type

00:15:48.001 --> 00:15:51.398
is passed to Resend, a transactional email

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:55.144
API, solely to deliver that one link.

00:15:55.919 --> 00:15:58.385
A short-lived cookie protects the

00:15:58.456 --> 00:15:59.968
redirect.

00:16:00.756 --> 00:16:03.555
This is the one cookie the

00:16:04.577 --> 00:16:08.140
entire Lolly system sets: lolly_ca_state,

00:16:08.198 --> 00:16:12.879
HttpOnly, scoped to /api/ca,

00:16:12.942 --> 00:16:15.469
expiring within ten minutes.

00:16:16.215 --> 00:16:19.253
It carries a random value, not a tracking

00:16:19.313 --> 00:16:22.626
identifier, and exists only to stop the

00:16:22.708 --> 00:16:25.670
OAuth redirect being forged.

00:16:26.429 --> 00:16:28.996
It is cleared as soon as sign-in

00:16:29.059 --> 00:16:30.318
completes.

00:16:31.106 --> 00:16:34.194
Your IP address is used, briefly, to

00:16:34.255 --> 00:16:36.533
prevent abuse of the sign-in

00:16:37.573 --> 00:16:40.287
endpoints «so one script can't spam an

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.794
inbox or exhaust the email quota».

00:16:44.588 --> 00:16:46.997
Lolly hashes it before creating a

00:16:47.144 --> 00:16:50.158
short-lived abuse-control bucket; the raw

00:16:50.219 --> 00:16:53.369
address is not sent to that store.

00:16:54.139 --> 00:16:57.033
The bucket expires after about a minute

00:16:57.109 --> 00:16:59.969
and is not used for tracking.

00:17:00.738 --> 00:17:03.876
Ordinary hosting access logs are separate

00:17:03.961 --> 00:17:06.119
and described below.

00:17:06.884 --> 00:17:08.971
The certificate service issues a

00:17:09.098 --> 00:17:12.769
short-lived certificate «7, 30, 90 or

00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:15.080
365

00:17:16.067 --> 00:17:18.656
days, your choice, capped by the

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:21.750
operator's policy» binding your verified

00:17:21.812 --> 00:17:24.654
email to the public half of the keypair

00:17:24.769 --> 00:17:27.270
generated on your device.

00:17:28.053 --> 00:17:30.494
The private half never leaves your

00:17:30.559 --> 00:17:31.868
browser.

00:17:32.681 --> 00:17:36.393
Nothing about the issuance is recorded.

00:17:37.182 --> 00:17:40.267
The certificate service keeps no

00:17:41.201 --> 00:17:43.795
issuance log: not your email, not the

00:17:43.856 --> 00:17:46.475
provider, not a serial number, not a

00:17:46.537 --> 00:17:47.969
timestamp.

00:17:48.773 --> 00:17:52.543
No database, no log line, no webhook.

00:17:53.353 --> 00:17:56.610
Your email address exists in the request

00:17:56.729 --> 00:17:59.298
only long enough to be written into the

00:17:59.361 --> 00:18:02.888
certificate that your own device receives,

00:18:02.951 --> 00:18:05.570
and then it is gone from our side

00:18:05.638 --> 00:18:07.094
entirely.

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:10.815
After that, signing is offline again for

00:18:10.874 --> 00:18:13.619
the certificate's whole lifetime.

00:18:14.395 --> 00:18:17.030
Exporting a file never contacts the

00:18:17.092 --> 00:18:20.969
certificate service - only enrolling did.

00:18:21.754 --> 00:18:24.768
The tradeoff, stated plainly.

00:18:25.544 --> 00:18:28.715
An earlier version of this service did log

00:18:28.793 --> 00:18:31.727
each issuance, so that a misissued or

00:18:31.802 --> 00:18:34.894
compromised certificate could be traced.

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:38.568
We removed it, because that log was the

00:18:38.661 --> 00:18:41.478
only place in all of Lolly where personal

00:18:41.538 --> 00:18:45.371
data came to rest on a server, and we

00:18:45.423 --> 00:18:47.661
would rather not hold it than hold it

00:18:47.727 --> 00:18:48.970
carefully.

00:18:49.748 --> 00:18:51.761
What we give up is server-side

00:18:51.824 --> 00:18:55.505
traceability: if a certificate is misused

00:18:55.569 --> 00:18:58.594
we cannot look up who obtained it.

00:18:59.369 --> 00:19:02.351
Certificates are short-lived by design - 7

00:19:02.439 --> 00:19:07.230
to 365 days, your choice, capped by the

00:19:07.292 --> 00:19:10.509
operator - and expire on their own, which

00:19:10.571 --> 00:19:13.995
is the mitigation we rely on instead.

00:19:14.777 --> 00:19:17.819
Self-hosters whose own obligations require

00:19:17.918 --> 00:19:21.418
an audit log can add one, and become the

00:19:21.478 --> 00:19:24.770
controller of that data by doing so.

00:19:25.909 --> 00:19:28.268
The browser extension

00:19:29.204 --> 00:19:32.617
The Lolly URL Screenshot browser extension

00:19:32.688 --> 00:19:35.908
does not collect, store or transmit any

00:19:35.972 --> 00:19:37.743
personal data.

00:19:38.531 --> 00:19:41.300
No analytics, no tracking, no remote

00:19:41.391 --> 00:19:42.494
server.

00:19:43.277 --> 00:19:44.994
What it does.

00:19:45.771 --> 00:19:47.852
When you ask the Lolly web app to

00:19:47.928 --> 00:19:51.959
screenshot a URL, the extension opens that

00:19:52.047 --> 00:19:54.825
page in a temporary background tab,

00:19:54.904 --> 00:19:57.419
captures it in your browser using the

00:19:57.482 --> 00:20:01.013
DevTools Protocol, hands the image back to

00:20:01.076 --> 00:20:03.744
the app and closes the tab.

00:20:04.502 --> 00:20:07.296
Everything happens locally, on your own

00:20:07.355 --> 00:20:09.369
device and network.

00:20:10.155 --> 00:20:11.411
Data.

00:20:12.212 --> 00:20:14.368
We collect nothing.

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:18.283
The extension has no servers and makes no

00:20:18.345 --> 00:20:19.294
network

00:20:20.301 --> 00:20:22.818
requests of its own.

00:20:23.568 --> 00:20:26.223
Captured images go straight to the Lolly

00:20:26.297 --> 00:20:28.756
app in the same browser - never

00:20:29.808 --> 00:20:32.817
uploaded by the extension.

00:20:33.587 --> 00:20:36.351
The URL'S you capture are used only to

00:20:36.412 --> 00:20:39.138
load that one page for that one

00:20:40.078 --> 00:20:41.516
screenshot.

00:20:42.308 --> 00:20:45.367
They are not logged or shared.

00:20:46.138 --> 00:20:47.693
Permissions.

00:20:48.463 --> 00:20:51.297
debugger - to capture the rendered page

00:20:51.364 --> 00:20:54.089
via the DevTools Protocol «the

00:20:55.091 --> 00:20:58.052
same mechanism the Lolly desktop app

00:20:58.115 --> 00:20:59.293
uses».

00:21:00.057 --> 00:21:03.168
tabs - to open and close the temporary tab

00:21:03.229 --> 00:21:05.194
the page loads in.

00:21:05.966 --> 00:21:08.366
Host access « » - because the page you

00:21:08.429 --> 00:21:10.760
choose to capture can be

00:21:11.586 --> 00:21:13.445
on any site.

00:21:14.211 --> 00:21:17.783
Chrome surfaces this at install time as a

00:21:17.874 --> 00:21:20.019
broad permission warning.

00:21:20.804 --> 00:21:24.544
The extension only ever visits the URL you

00:21:24.608 --> 00:21:25.818
give it.

00:21:26.628 --> 00:21:30.132
None of these are used to read, monitor or

00:21:30.194 --> 00:21:32.711
transmit your browsing beyond that one

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:34.669
requested capture.

00:21:35.796 --> 00:21:37.946
Infrastructure logs

00:21:38.943 --> 00:21:41.346
Like any website, the servers behind

00:21:41.405 --> 00:21:43.884
lolly-tools - and behind any Lolly

00:21:43.945 --> 00:21:46.670
deployment - generate standard web-server

00:21:46.738 --> 00:21:49.529
access logs whenever a request reaches

00:21:49.566 --> 00:21:53.202
them at all: IP address, requested path,

00:21:53.271 --> 00:21:55.669
timestamp, user agent.

00:21:56.438 --> 00:21:59.231
That's baseline hosting behaviour, not

00:21:59.296 --> 00:22:02.417
something Lolly adds on top, and it never

00:22:02.478 --> 00:22:05.421
contains the contents of your documents,

00:22:05.480 --> 00:22:08.071
because those never reach a server to

00:22:08.131 --> 00:22:09.544
begin with.

00:22:10.309 --> 00:22:12.976
The one deliberate exception is a file you

00:22:13.035 --> 00:22:17.259
explicitly hand to an MCP lolly_transform,

00:22:17.344 --> 00:22:20.373
lolly_verify or lolly_redact call, which

00:22:20.438 --> 00:22:22.963
is processed in memory and never written

00:22:23.052 --> 00:22:26.945
to disk or a log, as described above.

00:22:27.745 --> 00:22:30.680
Lolly's own code writes nothing to those

00:22:30.743 --> 00:22:31.868
logs.

00:22:32.650 --> 00:22:35.984
The MCP server contains no logging

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:37.993
statements at all.

00:22:38.761 --> 00:22:41.508
The certificate service emits exactly two

00:22:41.569 --> 00:22:44.320
lines, both on failure and both

00:22:44.390 --> 00:22:47.144
deliberately stripped: a send-failure

00:22:47.205 --> 00:22:50.548
status code with no recipient address, and

00:22:50.616 --> 00:22:53.185
an error message with no stack trace or

00:22:53.251 --> 00:22:56.238
URL «a stack could carry an enrolment

00:22:56.299 --> 00:22:57.469
token».

00:22:58.236 --> 00:23:01.017
Everything else in the log is the hosting

00:23:01.079 --> 00:23:03.444
platform's, not ours.

00:23:04.236 --> 00:23:07.279
For lolly-tools, hosting is Vercel and

00:23:07.355 --> 00:23:10.614
access-log retention follows Vercel's own

00:23:10.677 --> 00:23:13.743
platform defaults for our plan.

00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:17.796
We configure no log drain, no long-term

00:23:17.857 --> 00:23:20.806
log export and no analytics or monitoring

00:23:20.867 --> 00:23:22.595
product on top.

00:23:23.347 --> 00:23:26.459
We keep no copy of these logs ourselves,

00:23:26.513 --> 00:23:29.340
which also means we have no way to search

00:23:29.398 --> 00:23:31.895
them for you - see Your rights.

00:23:33.035 --> 00:23:36.524
Legal bases, retention and recipients

00:23:37.434 --> 00:23:40.739
Almost nothing here needs a legal basis,

00:23:40.799 --> 00:23:43.794
because almost nothing is processed.

00:23:44.571 --> 00:23:47.769
For completeness, the entire list:

00:23:48.557 --> 00:23:50.218
Recipients.

00:23:50.996 --> 00:23:54.027
The categories of recipient are: our

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.793
hosting provider «Vercel Inc.»

00:23:57.522 --> 00:24:00.399
; our abuse-control store provider, which

00:24:00.453 --> 00:24:03.409
receives only short-lived, one-way-derived

00:24:03.470 --> 00:24:07.287
bucket keys and never the raw IP address;

00:24:07.355 --> 00:24:10.114
and - only if you use the email sign-in

00:24:10.175 --> 00:24:13.223
option - a transactional email provider

00:24:13.286 --> 00:24:14.544
«Resend».

00:24:15.298 --> 00:24:18.798
If you sign in with GitHub, Google or SUSE

00:24:18.879 --> 00:24:21.877
«id-suse-com», you interact with that

00:24:21.936 --> 00:24:24.604
provider directly under their own privacy

00:24:24.664 --> 00:24:25.870
policy.

00:24:26.632 --> 00:24:29.974
They tell us a verified email address and

00:24:30.036 --> 00:24:31.469
nothing else.

00:24:32.250 --> 00:24:35.398
We share personal data with no one else,

00:24:35.459 --> 00:24:38.753
and we do not sell data, run advertising

00:24:38.804 --> 00:24:40.844
or profile users.

00:24:41.604 --> 00:24:44.619
Transfers outside the EEA.

00:24:45.416 --> 00:24:49.368
Vercel and Resend are US companies.

00:24:50.148 --> 00:24:52.916
Function compute for lolly-tools is pinned

00:24:53.013 --> 00:24:56.059
to Vercel's Frankfurt «fra1» region so

00:24:56.121 --> 00:24:59.504
processing happens in the EU, but as

00:24:59.566 --> 00:25:02.238
US-headquartered providers they may still

00:25:02.327 --> 00:25:06.344
access data as processors from the US.

00:25:07.123 --> 00:25:09.873
Those transfers rely on the European

00:25:09.934 --> 00:25:12.953
Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses

00:25:13.039 --> 00:25:17.565
and/or the EU-US Data Privacy Framework,

00:25:17.641 --> 00:25:20.162
as set out in each provider's data

00:25:20.223 --> 00:25:22.144
processing agreement.

00:25:22.901 --> 00:25:25.224
Because the personal data reaching these

00:25:25.285 --> 00:25:28.580
providers is so limited - an email address

00:25:28.655 --> 00:25:31.271
passed through to send one message,

00:25:31.338 --> 00:25:34.570
ordinary access logs, and a short-lived

00:25:34.630 --> 00:25:37.032
derived abuse-control bucket - the

00:25:37.113 --> 00:25:40.419
exposure is correspondingly small.

00:25:41.207 --> 00:25:44.268
Automated decision-making.

00:25:45.080 --> 00:25:46.089
None.

00:25:46.870 --> 00:25:50.000
There is no profiling and no automated

00:25:50.061 --> 00:25:53.076
decision producing legal or similarly

00:25:53.157 --> 00:25:55.519
significant effects «Art.

00:25:56.265 --> 00:25:57.968
22».

00:25:59.088 --> 00:26:01.094
Children's privacy

00:26:02.107 --> 00:26:04.400
Lolly does not knowingly collect personal

00:26:04.431 --> 00:26:08.269
information from anyone, of any age, in

00:26:08.329 --> 00:26:11.036
the ordinary course of using the app -

00:26:11.084 --> 00:26:13.470
there is nothing to collect.

00:26:14.245 --> 00:26:16.964
The one place personal information «an

00:26:17.054 --> 00:26:20.191
email address» is ever gathered is Content

00:26:20.253 --> 00:26:23.740
Credentials enrolment, described above,

00:26:23.798 --> 00:26:26.751
which is not directed at or intended for

00:26:26.812 --> 00:26:28.019
children.

00:26:29.171 --> 00:26:30.378
Your rights

00:26:31.238 --> 00:26:33.607
Because almost everything Lolly touches is

00:26:33.663 --> 00:26:36.646
stored only on your own device, most of

00:26:36.706 --> 00:26:39.085
what data-protection law calls "your

00:26:39.145 --> 00:26:41.563
rights" - access, correction, deletion,

00:26:41.622 --> 00:26:43.666
portability - are things you can already

00:26:43.725 --> 00:26:45.743
do yourself, instantly, without asking

00:26:45.803 --> 00:26:48.549
anyone: your data lives in your browser's

00:26:48.606 --> 00:26:51.268
storage, in a form you can inspect, export

00:26:51.320 --> 00:26:53.939
«Export my data & render everything,

00:26:54.004 --> 00:26:57.523
above» or delete «Profile → Clear all

00:26:58.361 --> 00:27:00.093
my data».

00:27:00.861 --> 00:27:04.664
Formally, under GDPR Articles 15 to 22 you

00:27:04.712 --> 00:27:06.795
have the right to access your personal

00:27:06.854 --> 00:27:10.544
data, to rectify it, to erase it, to

00:27:10.593 --> 00:27:12.777
restrict or object to its processing

00:27:12.833 --> 00:27:15.210
«including objecting to anything we base

00:27:15.243 --> 00:27:17.616
on legitimate interests», to data

00:27:17.676 --> 00:27:19.949
portability and - where processing rests

00:27:19.994 --> 00:27:22.429
on consent - to withdraw that consent at

00:27:22.486 --> 00:27:25.357
any time, without affecting the lawfulness

00:27:25.396 --> 00:27:28.295
of what happened before you withdrew it.

00:27:29.075 --> 00:27:32.305
Here is the honest position on exercising

00:27:32.368 --> 00:27:34.343
them against us.

00:27:35.123 --> 00:27:38.157
Since we no longer keep an issuance log,

00:27:38.216 --> 00:27:41.260
we hold no personal data about you that we

00:27:41.321 --> 00:27:44.820
can look up, correct, export or delete.

00:27:45.562 --> 00:27:48.206
If you write and ask what we have on you,

00:27:48.264 --> 00:27:50.823
the truthful answer is nothing, and we

00:27:50.881 --> 00:27:52.420
will say so.

00:27:53.192 --> 00:27:56.322
The one category that exists at all is

00:27:56.383 --> 00:27:59.459
hosting access logs keyed to an IP

00:27:59.519 --> 00:28:02.670
address, held by our hosting provider

00:28:02.751 --> 00:28:05.319
under their retention defaults.

00:28:06.085 --> 00:28:08.542
We have no facility to search or

00:28:08.634 --> 00:28:11.896
selectively delete those, and we will tell

00:28:11.984 --> 00:28:15.119
you that rather than pretend otherwise.

00:28:15.884 --> 00:28:18.581
Everything that is actually yours is on

00:28:18.647 --> 00:28:21.931
your device, where you can already read,

00:28:22.001 --> 00:28:24.617
export and destroy it without asking

00:28:24.700 --> 00:28:26.469
anyone's permission.

00:28:27.255 --> 00:28:30.244
You have the right to complain.

00:28:31.001 --> 00:28:33.231
If you think we have handled your data

00:28:33.291 --> 00:28:36.474
improperly, you can lodge a complaint with

00:28:36.538 --> 00:28:39.731
a data protection supervisory authority -

00:28:39.789 --> 00:28:43.185
in the EU, the authority in your country

00:28:43.228 --> 00:28:46.117
of residence, place of work or where you

00:28:46.175 --> 00:28:49.070
believe the infringement occurred «Art.

00:28:49.853 --> 00:28:51.769
77».

00:28:52.544 --> 00:28:55.432
Our lead supervisory authority is the

00:28:55.518 --> 00:28:57.428
Bayerisches Landesamt für

00:28:57.510 --> 00:29:00.787
Datenschutzaufsicht «BayLDA» in Ansbach,

00:29:00.848 --> 00:29:02.070
Germany.

00:29:02.840 --> 00:29:05.641
You do not need to contact us first,

00:29:05.700 --> 00:29:08.895
though we would like the chance to fix it.

00:29:09.685 --> 00:29:12.218
We don't sell data.

00:29:13.011 --> 00:29:15.867
We don't have any to sell.

00:29:16.979 --> 00:29:19.555
Changes to this policy

00:29:20.509 --> 00:29:23.476
The date at the top changes whenever this

00:29:23.540 --> 00:29:25.194
document does.

00:29:25.958 --> 00:29:28.294
A change that alters what leaves your

00:29:28.354 --> 00:29:31.189
device or what's retained gets its own

00:29:31.249 --> 00:29:34.638
line here, not a silent edit - if you want

00:29:34.721 --> 00:29:37.665
to see what changed, ask «below» or

00:29:37.726 --> 00:29:40.470
compare against the public source.

00:29:41.598 --> 00:29:45.225
Who is responsible, and how to reach us

00:29:46.285 --> 00:29:50.318
The data controller for lolly-tools is:

00:29:51.116 --> 00:29:54.862
SUSE Software Solutions Germany GmbH

00:29:54.971 --> 00:29:57.660
Frankenstraße 146

00:29:57.758 --> 00:30:02.228
90461 Nürnberg Germany

00:30:03.122 --> 00:30:05.926
SUSE has appointed a Data Protection

00:30:05.984 --> 00:30:10.244
Officer, reachable at privacy@suse-com.

00:30:11.030 --> 00:30:13.949
Use that address for any formal request

00:30:14.011 --> 00:30:16.319
under "Your rights" above.

00:30:17.104 --> 00:30:19.725
For anything about Lolly itself - how it

00:30:19.786 --> 00:30:23.291
works, why a thing is the way it is or a

00:30:23.352 --> 00:30:26.344
correction to this document - contact Andy

00:30:26.406 --> 00:30:29.644
Fitzsimon, fitzy@suse-com.

00:30:30.431 --> 00:30:33.303
For a self-hosted or enterprise Lolly

00:30:33.365 --> 00:30:36.430
instance, contact whoever operates it

00:30:36.488 --> 00:30:39.751
instead: the operator is the controller

00:30:39.864 --> 00:30:42.069
for their own deployment.

00:30:42.871 --> 00:30:46.043
SUSE and the Lolly open source project

00:30:46.131 --> 00:30:48.847
hold no data for deployments they don't

00:30:48.908 --> 00:30:49.919
run.
